    "summary": "High‑energy Utica show with soaring Here Comes Sunshine & monster Dark Star",
    "blurb": "The March 21 1973 performance delivers a punchy Bertha opener and an inspired Here Comes Sunshine. Highlights include a sprawling Dark Star > Eyes Of The World sequence and tight vocal harmonies on Me And Bobby McGee. Soundboard recordings capture the set in clear, high‑energy detail.",
    "review": "Utica Memorial Auditorium saw the Dead at a creative peak on March 21, 1973. After a rousing Bertha kickoff, the first set rolls through folk‑rock staples before bursting into Here Comes Sunshine, where Jerry’s lead lines sparkle over Bob’s louder‑in‑mix rhythm work. The second set builds momentum with a seamless Weather Report Prelude into an expansive Dark Star that mutates into Eyes Of The World and lands on Wharf Rat, showcasing Keith’s lush keyboards and Bill’s fluid drumming. Me And Bobby McGee offers heartfelt vocal harmonies, while China Cat Sunflower > I Know You Rider glides effortlessly, underscoring the band’s tight interplay throughout this high‑energy marathon.",
